       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one. Ibuprofen 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I can't find a clinical setting where that dose is appropriate. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular harm, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. Entering it myself would bypass the check that caught it, and I'm not comfortable doing that. It's your call to make as the attending, but I won't be the one to place it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily\n- 400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily\n- Another dose within labeled limits\n\nIf you believe the patient needs more than the labeled maximum, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy first. You could also enter the order yourself directly in the order system, where it will go through pharmacist verification. Tell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
